   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public officers law, in relation to waiving the residency\nrequirement for certain county attorney positions within Warren county",
    "basePrintNo": "S19",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S19-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Public Officers Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S19\n\nSPONSOR: STEC\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public officers law, in relation to waiving the\nresidency requirement for certain county attorney positions within\nWarren county\n\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo waive the residency requirements for certain assistant attorneys in\nWarren County.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 - Amends Section 3 of the public officers law to allow for\nnon-residents to serve as assistant district attorney, assistant public\ndefender or assistant county attorney within Warren County.\n\nSection 2 - Provides effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation comes at the request of the Warren County Board of\nSupervisors.\n\nFor years, the county has struggled to fill necessary and important\npositions due to a dearth of qualified individuals.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
